< **PS14 — A FOREIGN ARMY IN THE KINGDOM IS THE CROWN'S BUSINESS AS FAR AS THE CROWN'S HOLD REACHES.** Under `polityPrecedenceEnabled`, B's answer reads B's ONE foreign book with the new precedence class `passage_of_arms` (PL §3's table gains the row, the chair's at P4): the immediate liege's stance toward A at `POLITY_LIEGE_SHARE[band]` (PL4) and the paramount's at reach `r` by `polityHold` (PL5). A member that grants passage to its liege's ENEMY is PRICED AT ONCE as defiance (a `fealty_defied` row REQUESTED through PL's one door `requestFealtyRow` with the unit's registered episode prefix, PL7's spirit and RULINGS-ROUND2 A.14) — never a break, never forbidden [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — SEAMS-r2-10]. A member trespassed or invaded is a member whose liege owes PROTECTION (PL8): an `armed_incursion` into a member's land is an input on the polity's decided relief exactly as a siege is (PL §4.3's one relief decider, its war arm's gates) — and the liege's `sent` has a CARRIER: PS's incursion leaf takes the answer at first sight through PL's pure decider `reliefAnswerOf`, before the contest (it stands as an input line on the incursion card, PL §4.3, OD-PL-48), so a `sent` on this incursion adds the liege's relief share — as `computeAllyRelief` computes it, `ALLY_RELIEF_FRACTION` × the liege's field force — to the DEFENDER's side of the border contest at the member's border (§7.5; a PS-and-PL joint row); PL's fealty record keeps the ANSWER (`sent · kept`) and the OUTCOME, reading the outcome from THE PASSAGE's crossing [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — PL-V5 · RULINGS-ROUND3 A.6]. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — RULINGS-ROUND4 A.1 · A.2 · PS-W1 · R-PL: (1) THE CALL SUPPLIES A DEFAULT, NEVER A FACT — `reliefAnswerOf`'s answer at first sight is the DEFAULT of the incursion card's LIEGE LINE, carried on the crossing row's one declared sub-field `liegeAnswer` (`sent · kept`, §2.8); the DM may leave, tilt or decide that line in the hearing week like any line of the ca