WN RIDERS in a rebel member's land are a FOREIGN UNIT on this ladder, asked, refused or met in arms as any army, trespass by hostility included (§F.5). The hold is read at each placement, so a crown whose hold FALLS turns its members' right into a tolerance the week the holder believes it, and the FIRST VISIBLE sign of a break (requirement 16) is THE PASSAGE's own: a patrol turned back at a border it rode freely last season (§17 #20). No new stance word (the permit's `source` gains `banner`, a compound-scoped field value); armies are untouched (members' armies stand as allies by PL §4.5, the banner is the riders' only). Dark `polityHoldEnabled` (no hold read): the weak arm.
